tool_args.new_string:
OpenVLA shows 24--26/32 in the OXE-pretrained baseline with similar trained values (Appendix Figure~\ref{fig:cross_arch_l1}).
The variation across architectures reflects attention mechanism design: Phi-3-Vision's full MHA saturates all 32 heads, while Qwen2.5-VL's grouped-query attention with fewer key-value heads yields a lower baseline (13--14/16), indicating that head count and grouping strategy constrain L1 routing capacity.
\textbf{L1 instruction routing is an inherited backbone property, not a consequence of VLA training.}
